[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'turn this off. The prompt enhancer is going to take up more compute, and I don\'t think it\'s necessary. So, afterwards, after loading the models, the red outline and the errors should disappear. So, next, we can proceed to generate the video. Here are some'

[06:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'additional settings. So, for prompt enhance, this basically uses whatever model you have here to enhance your prompt further. But, of course, it\'s going to take up more time and compute, so I just tend to turn this off. And then, here\'s where you would set the'

[06:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'duration. Let\'s just keep it at 5 seconds, but this can do up to 20 seconds safely. You can probably even do longer if your hardware can handle it. And then, here is the frame rate. Here is where we would set the aspect ratio and then the resolution. And then, up'

[06:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here is where we would enter our prompts. I\'m just going to leave it at this prompt. Now, if you click this icon in the corner, it will expand the workflow. And let me just go over how this works in simple terms. Now, up here is where we can use the optional prompt'

[06:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'enhancer to edit the prompt further, but since we switched it off, this part would be disabled. It\'s actually first going to generate low resolution in the first pass, and then it\'s going to plug it through our upscaler. Remember, we'

[07:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'loaded a spatial upscaler over here. And that upscaler is basically going to upscale the video into our desired resolution. And that\'s what makes LTX generation so fast. It\'s because it first generates a low resolution video'

[07:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in its first pass, which is very quick, and then it uses an upscaler to generate the full resolution in the second pass. Anyway, that is how the workflow works. Next, let\'s press run to generate the video. All right, so you can see this'

[07:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'was very quick. It only took like 20 seconds to generate the video. And here\'s our result. All right, so that was text-to-video.'

